(5461750, 786801, 105747, '<td valign="top">Nicely done, maybe a little ripple,shadow or reflrction around the logs would  place them more down into the water. This may be the look you want, and if so it''s works great. Great shot, Good luck, Mike</td>', 'Nicely done, maybe a little ripple,shadow or reflrction around the logs would  place them more down into the water. This may be the look you want, and if so it''s works great. Great shot, Good luck, Mike', '2009-05-01 17:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(5461770, 786531, 105747, '<td valign="top">Great shot of landscape. I was told once, that if you have to point out the center of attention in a landscape shot, you need to recompose it to bring it out. I think it is the tree and how it contributes to the overall shot, but the clouds are a bit overwelming. Maybe the use of a filter when you shot the photo, or a gradient to soften the sky after you took the shot.  Good luck, Mike</td>', 'Great shot of landscape. I was told once, that if you have to point out the center of attention in a landscape shot, you need to recompose it to bring it out. I think it is the tree and how it contributes to the overall shot, but the clouds are a bit overwelming. Maybe the use of a filter when you shot the photo, or a gradient to soften the sky after you took the shot.  Good luck, Mike', '2009-05-01 17:14:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5461773, 786715, 105747, '<td valign="top">Great shot, I may have composed him a little to the right, and gave him room to jump, if he wanted to. Good luck, Mike</td>', 'Great shot, I may have composed him a little to the right, and gave him room to jump, if he wanted to. Good luck, Mike', '2009-05-01 17:16:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5461788, 785872, 105747, '<td valign="top">Great shot, although I don''t know exactly what the center of interest is. You could have used apature priority and used an f stop of f/11, and put everything in focus, or used a smaller f stop and focused on the pilings and let the front and back be a little out of focus. A little levels adjustment would probably have helped here. I love the Keys.  Good luck, Mike</td>', 'Great shot, although I don''t know exactly what the center of interest is. You could have used apature priority and used an f stop of f/11, and put everything in focus, or used a smaller f stop and focused on the pilings and let the front and back be a little out of focus. A little levels adjustment would probably have helped here. I love the Keys.  Good luck, Mike', '2009-05-01 17:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5461790, 785754, 105747, '<td valign="top">The work you did on this is great.  Great shot, Good luck, Mike</td>', 'The work you did on this is great.  Great shot, Good luck, Mike', '2009-05-01 17:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
