(5476128, 785668, 45475, '<td valign="top">Nope, no way in the world I would have guessed this! She''s gorgeous. Lovely portrait. You won the double in the commenting stakes too. Both Ed and Tom, congrats!</td>', 'Nope, no way in the world I would have guessed this! She''s gorgeous. Lovely portrait. You won the double in the commenting stakes too. Both Ed and Tom, congrats!', '2009-05-08 01:39:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476129, 786554, 69008, '<td valign="top">I like this just as it is, and do not understand why it didn''t place higher in the challenge results.  I think that it may be that the foreground flowers being a mix of colors like they are has something disruptive about it.  People seem to like bands of single colors, or layers if you call it that.  It''s a grand find, and excellent set up and shoot.  The "Poppin'' John" (J Deere) fans should like it as a print or poster.</td>', 'I like this just as it is, and do not understand why it didn''t place higher in the challenge results.  I think that it may be that the foreground flowers being a mix of colors like they are has something disruptive about it.  People seem to like bands of single colors, or layers if you call it that.  It''s a grand find, and excellent set up and shoot.  The "Poppin'' John" (J Deere) fans should like it as a print or poster.', '2009-05-08 01:40:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476132, 786967, 53814, '<td valign="top">Well-deserved recipient of the coveted Thumb. Teafrans'' comment seems somehow familiar.</td>', 'Well-deserved recipient of the coveted Thumb. Teafrans'' comment seems somehow familiar.', '2009-05-08 01:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476134, 780791, 69008, '<td valign="top">Just right, in every way. I like that you were able to keep the detail in the back of the dress, and the centered comp.</td>', 'Just right, in every way. I like that you were able to keep the detail in the back of the dress, and the centered comp.', '2009-05-08 01:43:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476135, 786866, 83313, '<td valign="top">Dang. I forgot to leave one of my comments about excessive JPEG compression. I can correct that oversight now, however. (You don''t get off that easy!) There are a ton of compression artifacts visible on and around the edges of the building. Your tiny file size of 37K reflect gobs of compression being used. When you save, always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (200k for this one)<br/> <br/>Added: It figures that the one time I overlook excessive compression, everybody else noticed it and commented on it!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-08 00:45:42.</i></td>', 'Dang. I forgot to leave one of my comments about excessive JPEG compression. I can correct that oversight now, however. (You don''t get off that easy!) There are a ton of compression artifacts visible on and around the edges of the building. Your tiny file size of 37K reflect gobs of compression being used. When you save, always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. (200k for this one) Added: It figures that the one time I overlook excessive compression, everybody else noticed it and commented on it!', '2009-05-08 01:44:03.000000', '2009-05-08 01:45:42.000000', 0),
(5476139, 786849, 3214, '<td valign="top">Love the whimsy and minimalistic feel!</td>', 'Love the whimsy and minimalistic feel!', '2009-05-08 01:45:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476140, 783841, 45475, '<td valign="top">Those rays are truly impressive. Strong finish, congrats!</td>', 'Those rays are truly impressive. Strong finish, congrats!', '2009-05-08 01:45:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476145, 786942, 3214, '<td valign="top">Nice finish on this one, Stacy, thought it would score higher though.</td>', 'Nice finish on this one, Stacy, thought it would score higher though.', '2009-05-08 01:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476146, 786821, 62357, '<td valign="top">I think <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=88136" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">JDubsgirl</a> pretty much hit the nail on the head.  For me, the B&amp;W conversion is really lacking.  It is full of very mid-tone grey and very little real black or white, making, as Juliet says in her comment, the feather blend in with the background.  Both comments made about the composition are also very valid.  I think it needs more space around the subject, as it feels pretty cramped.</td>', 'I think  JDubsgirl pretty much hit the nail on the head.  For me, the B&W conversion is really lacking.  It is full of very mid-tone grey and very little real black or white, making, as Juliet says in her comment, the feather blend in with the background.  Both comments made about the composition are also very valid.  I think it needs more space around the subject, as it feels pretty cramped.', '2009-05-08 01:48:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476148, 784766, 68504, '<td valign="top">Way, way too much fun!</td>', 'Way, way too much fun!', '2009-05-08 01:51:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476150, 785243, 45475, '<td valign="top">Not only held onto the 6, but climbed an extra 0.1! Awesome stuff.<br/> <br/>Next time you shoot a famous person, you really ought to put their name in the title ;)</td>', 'Not only held onto the 6, but climbed an extra 0.1! Awesome stuff. Next time you shoot a famous person, you really ought to put their name in the title ;)', '2009-05-08 01:52:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476152, 786821, 83313, '<td valign="top">It didn''t come up for me in voting, or I would tell you what I gave it. My impression is a lack of something that keeps the feather from standing out against the background. Could possibly be the heavy patterns of both the feather and the background, or maybe contrast also plays a part. They are different, but maybe not different enough. What does it look like in color?</td>', 'It didn''t come up for me in voting, or I would tell you what I gave it. My impression is a lack of something that keeps the feather from standing out against the background. Could possibly be the heavy patterns of both the feather and the background, or maybe contrast also plays a part. They are different, but maybe not different enough. What does it look like in color?', '2009-05-08 01:58:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476154, 785008, 68504, '<td valign="top">I like it too.</td>', 'I like it too.', '2009-05-08 01:59:32.000000', NULL, 0),
