(5476351, 786978, 74588, '<td valign="top">thats called making whoopie<br/>what a big feet she has:]</td>', 'thats called making whoopiewhat a big feet she has:]', '2009-05-08 07:45:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476353, 782259, 30982, '<td valign="top">A beautiful natural portrait, Jelena!  Very well done.</td>', 'A beautiful natural portrait, Jelena!  Very well done.', '2009-05-08 07:51:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476354, 786576, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very interesting view of the place!  You have quite the collection going of this scene.  My only suggestion would be to have the not-as-in-focus on the left, even though you say you didn''t want it there for the eye to find first, but I think the eye (for most English speaking folks) starts in the upper right third.  Or that could just be me - I do tend to be a bit backwards.</td>', 'Very interesting view of the place!  You have quite the collection going of this scene.  My only suggestion would be to have the not-as-in-focus on the left, even though you say you didn''t want it there for the eye to find first, but I think the eye (for most English speaking folks) starts in the upper right third.  Or that could just be me - I do tend to be a bit backwards.', '2009-05-08 07:53:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476355, 786978, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great view - did you bring the model or borrow her from someone else''s shoot?  I like to think she''s just there and you happened upon her.  ''Grats on the score and top 20 in a FS.  And no 1s, 2s, or 3s!</td>', 'Great view - did you bring the model or borrow her from someone else''s shoot?  I like to think she''s just there and you happened upon her.  ''Grats on the score and top 20 in a FS.  And no 1s, 2s, or 3s!', '2009-05-08 07:54:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476356, 786967, 30982, '<td valign="top">Dude - a thumb!!  Way cool.  Even better are the words that accompany it.</td>', 'Dude - a thumb!!  Way cool.  Even better are the words that accompany it.', '2009-05-08 07:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476357, 785046, 30982, '<td valign="top">New top 5 entry!!  Congrats!!!  You did a really nice job with this.</td>', 'New top 5 entry!!  Congrats!!!  You did a really nice job with this.', '2009-05-08 07:56:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476358, 785532, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very good use of the angle and the high keyishness in this.</td>', 'Very good use of the angle and the high keyishness in this.', '2009-05-08 07:57:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476359, 782465, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done portrait, though I am not a huge fan of the desat.  I do realize, though, that lots of folks like this kind of thing, particularly for bridal portraits.  You did a very good job of catching a natural, warm expression - and that counts for a lot!</td>', 'Very nicely done portrait, though I am not a huge fan of the desat.  I do realize, though, that lots of folks like this kind of thing, particularly for bridal portraits.  You did a very good job of catching a natural, warm expression - and that counts for a lot!', '2009-05-08 07:58:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476360, 786973, 30982, '<td valign="top">Sweet detail!!  Lovely use of that lens, and as Bob noted, excellent work with the exposure as yellow is very hard to shoot accurately.  What was your aperture for this?</td>', 'Sweet detail!!  Lovely use of that lens, and as Bob noted, excellent work with the exposure as yellow is very hard to shoot accurately.  What was your aperture for this?', '2009-05-08 08:00:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476361, 785421, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very cool!!  What a great find and what an awesome kite!  Very cooperative sky, too!</td>', 'Very cool!!  What a great find and what an awesome kite!  Very cooperative sky, too!', '2009-05-08 08:00:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476362, 785580, 30982, '<td valign="top">Doing his best impression of a peacock, I take it?  Love the pose and the way the bird is framed so nicely by the foliage.</td>', 'Doing his best impression of a peacock, I take it?  Love the pose and the way the bird is framed so nicely by the foliage.', '2009-05-08 08:01:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476363, 779010, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great timing and excellent framing!  I like the concentration and the light on the pitcher''s face, and the hint of blur in his hand.</td>', 'Great timing and excellent framing!  I like the concentration and the light on the pitcher''s face, and the hint of blur in his hand.', '2009-05-08 08:02:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476364, 786711, 30982, '<td valign="top">Really like the light in this - just right.</td>', 'Really like the light in this - just right.', '2009-05-08 08:04:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476365, 785692, 30982, '<td valign="top">I saw Penny''s shot first and thought maybe it was yours, but then saw this one, recognized the style in titling and the use of foreground detail and thought THIS one was yours.  You guys can''t confuse me like that!  Processing may be overdone for some tastes, but suits this image well, I think.</td>', 'I saw Penny''s shot first and thought maybe it was yours, but then saw this one, recognized the style in titling and the use of foreground detail and thought THIS one was yours.  You guys can''t confuse me like that!  Processing may be overdone for some tastes, but suits this image well, I think.', '2009-05-08 08:05:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476366, 782880, 30982, '<td valign="top">This has an excellent balance to it, in my opinion, and the gray suits your subject very well.  I quite like the city off to the left, the posts leading to it.  Works for me.</td>', 'This has an excellent balance to it, in my opinion, and the gray suits your subject very well.  I quite like the city off to the left, the posts leading to it.  Works for me.', '2009-05-08 08:07:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476367, 784495, 30982, '<td valign="top">Truly a lovely scene - poppies, green field, and an awesome sky on top of it all.  Great job with the composition and exposure, and congrats on a good score and placing in a FS.  I think the sharpening worked fine (not overdone) and I really like the use of the wide white border for this shot.  Nice work!</td>', 'Truly a lovely scene - poppies, green field, and an awesome sky on top of it all.  Great job with the composition and exposure, and congrats on a good score and placing in a FS.  I think the sharpening worked fine (not overdone) and I really like the use of the wide white border for this shot.  Nice work!', '2009-05-08 08:09:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476369, 786794, 30982, '<td valign="top">Excellent candid - love the looks you caught here!  And the sign is a wonderful inclusion into the scene.</td>', 'Excellent candid - love the looks you caught here!  And the sign is a wonderful inclusion into the scene.', '2009-05-08 08:11:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476370, 786194, 86447, '<td valign="top">I''s so glad this was you!   I wondered, since it reminded me of your daughter''s half face photo. Lovely!  Congrats on a 6+ in FS!</td>', 'I''s so glad this was you!   I wondered, since it reminded me of your daughter''s half face photo. Lovely!  Congrats on a 6+ in FS!', '2009-05-08 08:12:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476371, 784491, 30982, '<td valign="top">The greens in this are wonderful!  Great shot of this guy.</td>', 'The greens in this are wonderful!  Great shot of this guy.', '2009-05-08 08:13:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476375, 786897, 65234, '<td valign="top">ISO 12,800?!  Well, that certainly explains the noise ;-)</td>', 'ISO 12,800?!  Well, that certainly explains the noise ;-)', '2009-05-08 08:18:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476379, 779902, 82707, '<td valign="top">Fabulous shot!  It''s an awkward bird, but the image is not, and you got robbed on this one.</td>', 'Fabulous shot!  It''s an awkward bird, but the image is not, and you got robbed on this one.', '2009-05-08 08:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476381, 782345, 89341, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote but I think I would have been going for the 5 button.<br/> <br/>The first thing I notice is the halos around the chimneys which are distracting and the sky is a little too dark for the rest of the lighting and a little noisy (you could just select the sky (allowed in advanced only) and run a heavy noise routine on it depending what software you are using).<br/> <br/>The rest of the scene is just a tiny bit over processed for my tastes and I''d just like it to be toned down a fraction. The lighting on the building is uneven which looks like more halo effect (though I could be wrong) maybe you could post your original? Maybe turning up the light smoothing in the HDR software.<br/> <br/>The text on the sign leads you straight out of the photo, it would be better (though maybe not possible) to have the whole shot reversed so the text would be on the left and lead you into the shot.<br/> <br/>I think the whole crop is a little tight, especially on the awning, the awning blends into the building behind. Maybe slightly wider or even fill the frame more with the awning. Maybe a different angle, I find the shot is a bit flat, maybe the street going off into the distance would lead you into the shot more and give a more 3d feel to it.<br/> <br/>all IMHO of course!</td>', 'I didn''t vote but I think I would have been going for the 5 button. The first thing I notice is the halos around the chimneys which are distracting and the sky is a little too dark for the rest of the lighting and a little noisy (you could just select the sky (allowed in advanced only) and run a heavy noise routine on it depending what software you are using). The rest of the scene is just a tiny bit over processed for my tastes and I''d just like it to be toned down a fraction. The lighting on the building is uneven which looks like more halo effect (though I could be wrong) maybe you could post your original? Maybe turning up the light smoothing in the HDR software. The text on the sign leads you straight out of the photo, it would be better (though maybe not possible) to have the whole shot reversed so the text would be on the left and lead you into the shot. I think the whole crop is a little tight, especially on the awning, the awning blends into the building behind. Maybe slightly wider or even fill the frame more with the awning. Maybe a different angle, I find the shot is a bit flat, maybe the street going off into the distance would lead you into the shot more and give a more 3d feel to it. all IMHO of course!', '2009-05-08 08:28:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476391, 786610, 12998, '<td valign="top">This is just totally awesome!!!!!!!!  Very well done.</td>', 'This is just totally awesome!!!!!!!!  Very well done.', '2009-05-08 08:33:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476394, 785966, 73942, '<td valign="top">very pretty, love how the light falls on the rose</td>', 'very pretty, love how the light falls on the rose', '2009-05-08 08:35:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476396, 786670, 3724, '<td valign="top">chair and lilacs - very appealing rustic still-life</td>', 'chair and lilacs - very appealing rustic still-life', '2009-05-08 08:38:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476406, 786977, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is really gorgeous, Penny.  Very clean and crisp, perfectly composed.  Congrats on a great score and a new personal best, too!</td>', 'This is really gorgeous, Penny.  Very clean and crisp, perfectly composed.  Congrats on a great score and a new personal best, too!', '2009-05-08 08:59:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476407, 782345, 82707, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I would have waviered between a 5-6.  ...I love the detail metal lace ironwork (I''m sure it''s got an engineering name that I don''t know).  The ironwork is the softness in the image, and make a nice contrast against the brickwork.<br/> <br/>The negatives for me are;  the main focus is the sign, which is, just, not that interesting. If the lights underneath it were alight, it would have illuminated it.....and for my taste it is over saturated....too much colour....on the bricks &amp; the garden, and on the sky.<br/> <br/>Remember JMHO, and I have learnt a lot from people who don''t know it all, they just know what they like.....and are willing to tell you what and why....and they are the voters...<br/> <br/>PS I''m hanging out to get a HDR program.....so... enjoy playing....and remember to have fun, and it''s all just pixels....:)<br/></td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I would have waviered between a 5-6.  ...I love the detail metal lace ironwork (I''m sure it''s got an engineering name that I don''t know).  The ironwork is the softness in the image, and make a nice contrast against the brickwork. The negatives for me are;  the main focus is the sign, which is, just, not that interesting. If the lights underneath it were alight, it would have illuminated it.....and for my taste it is over saturated....too much colour....on the bricks & the garden, and on the sky. Remember JMHO, and I have learnt a lot from people who don''t know it all, they just know what they like.....and are willing to tell you what and why....and they are the voters... PS I''m hanging out to get a HDR program.....so... enjoy playing....and remember to have fun, and it''s all just pixels....:)', '2009-05-08 09:01:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476410, 783068, 3724, '<td valign="top">Very beautiful classic architectural rendering - your subject shown w/marvelous visual/optical compression. A compelling standout and favorite in this open challenge.</td>', 'Very beautiful classic architectural rendering - your subject shown w/marvelous visual/optical compression. A compelling standout and favorite in this open challenge.', '2009-05-08 09:04:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476415, 780113, 100831, '<td valign="top">Excellent! IMHO, this is one of your best buggy pictures - along with the title it just really works out well for content and execution. Great job, Lydia!</td>', 'Excellent! IMHO, this is one of your best buggy pictures - along with the title it just really works out well for content and execution. Great job, Lydia!', '2009-05-08 09:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476419, 786799, 100831, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous colors!! Way to win - congratulations!!</td>', 'Gorgeous colors!! Way to win - congratulations!!', '2009-05-08 09:07:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5476428, 784183, 87808, '<td valign="top">Urrrrrrrrhhhhhhhhhhuuuuuuuuuuh. )**%#)( #%*)# ##%Y@)%#&amp;^)#<br/> <br/>Well done sweetheart, a great shot, I am thrilled for you!</td>', 'Urrrrrrrrhhhhhhhhhhuuuuuuuuuuh. )**%#)( #%*)# ##%Y@)%#&^)# Well done sweetheart, a great shot, I am thrilled for you!', '2009-05-08 09:15:03.000000', NULL, 0),
