(5477508, 785845, 77196, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot of an Auburn Supercharged! If you ever get a chance to be in Auburn Indiana on Labor Day weekend, they have a Parade of Classics, including Auburns, Cords, and Duesenbergs - at the end of the parade, they park them around courthouse square and down the side streets - great photo ops! (Or, if you want to join the ACD Club ($50 annual dues, I believe), you can see them in the park as the owners prep them for the parade. )<br/></td>', 'Beautiful shot of an Auburn Supercharged! If you ever get a chance to be in Auburn Indiana on Labor Day weekend, they have a Parade of Classics, including Auburns, Cords, and Duesenbergs - at the end of the parade, they park them around courthouse square and down the side streets - great photo ops! (Or, if you want to join the ACD Club ($50 annual dues, I believe), you can see them in the park as the owners prep them for the parade. )', '2009-05-08 21:43:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5477519, 786799, 59267, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everybody for the comments! The dynamic range of this back-lighting scene is out of the capability of JPG but luckily is still in the range of RAW, therefore,  I didn''t use multi frame. The shutter was so slow because I used CPL and ISO 100 and with needs of DOF, big thanks to the pilots of the hot air balloons, they held the balloons still so there was no motion blur. LOL I think they held still for their riders to photograph tulips from above but I also took this advantage.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-06-24 00:59:18.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everybody for the comments! The dynamic range of this back-lighting scene is out of the capability of JPG but luckily is still in the range of RAW, therefore,  I didn''t use multi frame. The shutter was so slow because I used CPL and ISO 100 and with needs of DOF, big thanks to the pilots of the hot air balloons, they held the balloons still so there was no motion blur. LOL I think they held still for their riders to photograph tulips from above but I also took this advantage.', '2009-05-08 21:59:26.000000', '2009-06-24 01:59:18.000000', 0),
