(5478769, 782345, 39057, '<td valign="top">Looking at this again I would say:<br/> <br/>You may want to go back out to that spot with a tripod and just do an HDR on that building w/o the sign in the foreground. The ironwork, the hanging plants, the windows, and the bricks are perfect for this type of shot. <br/> <br/>I would use a wider angle on the lens...18mm. Get as much of the building in as possible. Keep the angle on the building about the same...maybe move a little more to your "left" and shoot towards the right. <br/> <br/>I live in N.O. - I may take a shot at it myself one day.</td>', 'Looking at this again I would say: You may want to go back out to that spot with a tripod and just do an HDR on that building w/o the sign in the foreground. The ironwork, the hanging plants, the windows, and the bricks are perfect for this type of shot.  I would use a wider angle on the lens...18mm. Get as much of the building in as possible. Keep the angle on the building about the same...maybe move a little more to your "left" and shoot towards the right.  I live in N.O. - I may take a shot at it myself one day.', '2009-05-10 00:11:21.000000', NULL, 0),
