(5729667, 782345, 63218, '<td valign="top">Yes! I do like this one. I can''t explain why I like this style of HDR, I just do. They remind me a little of Norman Rockwell illustrations. Very optimistic &amp; upbeat &amp; idealized. Sorry it didn''t do better. Not sure how I feel about editing out the people. I like people in the shot, but it''s hard to get a good artistic grouping. But they do add a sense of scale, which I like. I think you met your own goals which is what counts.  Since the print is selling, that means you have captured the way people feel about this street scene, so ur doin it rite. Keep on clickin''! "D<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-11-16 21:51:18.</i></td>', 'Yes! I do like this one. I can''t explain why I like this style of HDR, I just do. They remind me a little of Norman Rockwell illustrations. Very optimistic & upbeat & idealized. Sorry it didn''t do better. Not sure how I feel about editing out the people. I like people in the shot, but it''s hard to get a good artistic grouping. But they do add a sense of scale, which I like. I think you met your own goals which is what counts.  Since the print is selling, that means you have captured the way people feel about this street scene, so ur doin it rite. Keep on clickin''! "D', '2009-11-16 19:55:52.000000', '2009-11-16 21:51:18.000000', 0),
(5735140, 786208, 61961, '<td valign="top">Love that water color, and how the eye follows the river back to the sea.  Nice perspective, too.  Overall it may be a little oversaturated for my taste (e.g., blobs of red in the tree), but it does make an impact!</td>', 'Love that water color, and how the eye follows the river back to the sea.  Nice perspective, too.  Overall it may be a little oversaturated for my taste (e.g., blobs of red in the tree), but it does make an impact!', '2009-11-20 16:18:57.000000', NULL, 0),
